WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.520
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:04.196
KARL ROVE: Politics has
constantly been changing.

00:00:04.196 --> 00:00:05.570
DAVID AXELROD:
It's exhilarating.

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:08.440
It can be exasperating.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:11.564
Truth is that Karl and I don't
see eye to eye on some things.

00:00:11.564 --> 00:00:12.980
 We'll just keep
this between us,

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.146
but I actually like the guy.

00:00:14.146 --> 00:00:16.279
 There goes my career.

00:00:16.279 --> 00:00:18.820
KARL ROVE: Reagan used to say
that our American democracy was

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:22.780
always one generation
away from extinction.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:26.460
DAVID AXELROD: We're more
polarized now than ever.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:27.460
 That's understandable.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.550
We're in a tribal moment.

00:00:32.182 --> 00:00:33.740
DAVID AXELROD: In
a great campaign,

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:36.452
you have a very clear
sense of what it's about.

00:00:36.452 --> 00:00:38.160
KARL ROVE: A lot of
the campaign is going

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:39.840
to depend upon the message.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.910
 Donald Trump was
the anti-Obama.

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:44.450
 He held himself out as,
I'm going to take a brick

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:46.470
and throw it through
the plate glass window.

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:47.929
 Mission accomplished.

00:00:47.929 --> 00:00:49.470
If you're in a
campaign and you don't

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:50.920
believe you're going
to make a mistake,

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:52.290
you're in the wrong business.

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:54.150
The lesson is, when
you're attacked,

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:58.380
respond, impeach the charge, and
then go back on the offensive.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:00.795
 I have as much experience
as Jack Kennedy did.

00:01:00.795 --> 00:01:02.500
 Senator, you're
no Jack Kennedy.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:03.100
[LAUGHTER]

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:03.780
KARL ROVE: Pow!

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.900
Right there.

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:07.811
 These are battles
of definition.

00:01:07.811 --> 00:01:09.560
KARL ROVE: Each
candidate's trying to say,

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:11.842
I'm the answer to your
question in this election.

00:01:11.842 --> 00:01:12.800
DAVID AXELROD: Exactly.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:14.210
It's a performance.

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:16.760
And look at the campaigns
in the 19th century.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:17.910
And they were brutal.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:21.090
They just weren't on television.

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:24.770
The one corrective in a
democracy is the vote.

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:28.132
 Our moment is now.

00:01:28.132 --> 00:01:30.340
KARL ROVE: If you've never
been involved in politics,

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:31.660
don't be afraid to get started.

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:33.201
DAVID AXELROD: It
is really important

00:01:33.201 --> 00:01:35.200
to be agents of change.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.560
KARL ROVE: Politics is a
wonderful, noble profession,

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:42.190
and it ought to be the passion
of every single American.

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:46.210
DAVID AXELROD: If you want
change, this is your choice.

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:47.880
 Well said.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:49.930
DAVID AXELROD:
I'm David Axelrod.

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:51.400
 I'm Karl Rove.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:54.330
BOTH: And this is
our MasterClass.

